        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How do I fix an E01 error on a WalkingPad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              WalkingPad says E01 is a drive communication error. Turn the pad off, unplug it for about 10 minutes and restart; its FAQ notes E codes can be caused by transport. If E01 returns, contact WalkingPad support.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What does SAFE mean on a WalkingPad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              SAFE means the safety key is not inserted. Insert the red key fully into the handrail; if it is already in and SAFE stays, remove it, reinsert it and restart the pad.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why does my WalkingPad say Rest?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Rest appears after extended use. WalkingPad says its walking pads stop after about one hour of continuous use and its treadmills after about two; turn it off and let it cool for about 30 minutes before restarting.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I pair a WalkingPad remote?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Fit a fresh battery (CR2032 on most remotes, two AAA on the P1 and C1). Then, depending on the model, press the mode switch within five seconds of turning the pad on, or wait for the white progress bar and press the function button five to eight times.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I center a WalkingPad belt?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the C2 and A1 Pro, hold the remote’s mode and speed-up buttons for three seconds to enter CALI mode, then turn the rear screw on the side the belt drifts towards a half turn clockwise. The X21 manual specifies a quarter turn.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How often should I lubricate a WalkingPad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              About every three months at normal use, according to WalkingPad, with silicone treadmill lubricant. Its troubleshooting article gives 5 to 10 ml and its lubrication guide 1 to 2 drops, so start small and check that the deck is no longer dry.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

